  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, the highest-priority question is whether basic multimodal fusion provides any signal over single-modality baselines, and what a reasonable 'floor' for multimodal performance looks like. config_011 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, no aggregation, concat) is the simplest multimodal configuration: it uses the most standard RNA encoder (scvi_n200), a lightweight and well-established image encoder (resnet50), no profile aggregation, and the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the core question—does combining RNA and image representations via basic concatenation help?—without confounding from multiprofile aggregation, transformer pooling, or weighted fusion. Establishing this baseline first lets every subsequent experiment be interpreted as a controlled addition of complexity (e.g., multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, or stronger encoders), making the search trajectory maximally informative under a limited budget."
}

